mmodious like you netted  emic of addiction to opioids the opioid  overdose epidemic is killing as many as  91 Americans a day according to the  Center for Disease Control many doctors  have been arrested for running so-called  pill mills and turning patients into  addicts the DEA in the Hamilton Boone  Drug Task Force arrested 11 people dr.  Richard R an arrested in San Francisco  don't roll over fatigue under a reactor  was arrested along with 12 and in 2016  the DEA clamped down on painkillers  reducing the allowed production of  opioid medications by 25 percent or more  this year the CDC issued guidelines  advising doctors to avoid prescribing  high doses over 90 morphine milligram  equivalents so maybe it's no surprise  that it's a boundary pusher like tenant  who's one of the last doctors in America  willing to take patients who say they  need a high dose of pain medication to  function the rare cases in the other  states are really very dish cast out  totally tenant is never shied from the  public spotlight in addition to briefly  serving as mayor of his city he ran some  of Los Angeles County's earliest  methadone clinics to treat heroin  addicts and in the late 80s served as a  drug adviser for the NFL NASCAR and the  Los Angeles Dodgers controversy swirled  around him in many of these roles he  angered the NFL when he publicly  disclosed plans to monitor several New  England Patriots players for drug use  one NASCAR racer even accused him of  colluding to falsified drug tests to  target him after resigning Tennant told  the New York Times that no mistakes were  ever made during his time in politics  Tennant was instrumental in pushing  forward the pain patients Bill of Rights  in California which explicitly spells  out that opiates can be a safe and  effective form of pain treatment Tennant  acknowledges that opioids were over  prescribed in the past and should  generally be a last resort for pain  treatment but he believes the media and  government  now gone too far in demonizing them and  it's legitimate pain patients who are  paying the price once you start opioid  drugs this idea that you can just quit  them and it's your pain will gold  magically go away is a mist there are  people who can take opioid drug at a  very high dose for many years they've  the first doctors who ever said our goal  is to relieve your pain every other  doctor had said our goal is to get you  off any opioid medications the pressure  has even affected the way doctors think  about pain the American Medical  Association recommended in 2016 the  doctors no longer ask patients to rate  their pain I take the Hippocratic oath  services and my job is to relieve pain  and suffering so when I see somebody  like the AMA decide they're not going to  assess pain I'm not with them in a  recent New England Journal of Medicine  article one of the pain specialists who  advised the CDC on their guidelines  recommended that pain patients use  coping and acceptance strategies that  primarily reduce the suffering  associated with pain and only  secondarily reduce pain intensity that  pain is psychological  that needs to go out the window let me  tell you why because you're looking at  the guy he's probably done most of the  studies I start checking out with viral  titers autoimmune tests we find  biochemical physiological changes in the  body and we can now track down where  that's coming from  so these people who are being labeled  psychological is just a ploy to not  treat the patient and to try to blame  the patient rather than the medical  system who is rejecting them yet an  underreported fact is that pain patients  aren't the problem when it comes to  opioid abuse and addiction in America a  study from the Cochrane review found  that when legitimate pain patients are  screened for prior addiction issues  fewer than 1% ever become addicted to  opioids they're trying to give the idea  that we can't tell the difference  between the addict and the legitimate  pain patient simply not true it's easy  to do Tennant's believes the country  needs more pain specialists like him who  are willing to take the difficult cases  and challenge the emerging conventional  wisdom that opioids can't treat pain the  effort to completely discredit opioids  is a legitimate treatment option he says  will only lead to more pain resentment  and tragedy you just can't throw  legitimate good solid citizens who have  pain start calling them addicts and  start calling them subs abuse orders  disorders and you're starting to develop  great resentment in these people against  their government against the media I  consider the intentional removal of  effective pain medication it's a  deliberate action to inflict pain on  someone that's the definition of torture  we're tired of the battle tired of  fighting with the insurance companies  tired of fighting with the doctors to  describe what we go through every day  the suffering is inhumane  and this is just a medication to treat  pain it is not the first line of  medication when I read the CBC  guidelines and other government  issuances when I hear the politician  speak it says bill people like him do  not exist at all it's as though you're  invisible  [Music]  [Music]
 

